    <solution><p>Rewrite the first term using a negative exponent and use the chain rule on the logarithm:</p>
<p><me>\begin{aligned}
          \frac{d}{dx}\left(7x^{-5}-\ln(2x+1)\right)
          \amp = -35x^{-5-1}
          -\frac{2}{2x+1}.
          \end{aligned}</me></p>
